course: dictionary
lesson: 10956
title: Walkway: a path for walking
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A walkway is a path made for people to walk along. Its name gives you the clue: walk, and way. Walkways are often raised, covered, or built between buildings.
explain: «Machines are strong and fast and cannot see you, so factories are full of fences, guards and big red stop buttons, and visitors keep to the marked walkways.» The word marked tells you the walkways are shown clearly, so visitors stay where it is safe. Walkways are for people, not for machines.
explain: «A moving walkway is a flat belt without steps, often at airports; watch for the end, where it warns you.» A moving walkway carries you along, so you can stand still and let it move you. Ask: what word would fit here? Path would fit, so walkway means a path for walking.
fact: A walkway is a path or passage for people to walk along.
fact: Walkways are often raised, covered, or built between buildings.
fact: A «moving walkway» is a flat belt that carries people along, often at airports.
fact: A «boardwalk» is a walkway over wet ground, such as a marsh or a beach.
fact: Safety tip: keep to the marked walkways, walk and don't run, and hold the rails on a raised walkway.
exercise: What is a walkway? | A deep channel of water in the sea | A tall fence around a factory | A machine that lifts heavy pallets | *A path or passage for people to walk along
exercise: «A moving walkway is a flat belt without steps, often at airports.» Where would you most often find one? | *At an airport | Deep in a forest | Inside a school bag | Under the sea
exercise: «Forklifts are quiet and turn sharply, so near them people keep to the marked walkways.» Why do people keep to the walkways near forklifts? | To look at the pallets | Because forklifts cannot move | *To stay safe from the machine | To get a faster ride
test: A «boardwalk» is a walkway over what kind of ground? | Hard rock | *Wet ground | Dry sand | Ice only
test: «Swimming straight against a rip can be like running the wrong way on a moving walkway.» What does this tell you about a moving walkway? | It is always under water | *It carries you along, so going against it is hard | It has steps you must climb | It can only be found in parks
exam: On a raised walkway, what is the safe thing to do? | Stop in the middle to take photos | Climb over the rails to see the view | Run fast to get across quickly | *Walk, not run, and hold the rails
